 * shopping_mall_ai_coupon_events.
 *
 * Retrieve all coupon event records for a given coupon. The endpoint queries
 * the shopping_mall_ai_coupon_events table and returns all event entries
 * related to the provided couponId. Event types include issuance, redemption,
 * expiration, or admin audit actions, each capturing event type, timestamp, and
 * involved actor details as per schema.
 *
 * API access is typically allowed to seller (if their own coupon), admin, or
 * system auditor. Data returned include event types, timestamps, affected
 * customer/order references, and any associated audit details. Sensitive
 * details may be filtered depending on the requesting role. Pagination is
 * recommended for large record counts, and access logs should be maintained for
 * compliance.
 *
 * If the coupon does not exist or the user lacks permission for this coupon's
 * context, an error is returned.
 *
 * @param props - Request properties
 * @param props.seller - The authenticated seller
 * @param props.couponId - ID of the target coupon whose events are to be listed
 * @returns Paginated coupon event logs for the specified coupon (first 100
 *   records)
 * @throws {Error} If the coupon does not exist or the seller does not own the
