 * (e.g., card, deposit), amount, status, timestamps for initiation (and
 * optionally resolution), and payment channel context.
 *
 * OrderId (from path) must reference an existing order. The endpoint is used by
 * fulfillment, admin, or reconciliation workflows—customers typically do not
 * invoke directly.
 *
 * Business logic checks for multi-method usage, matches payment sums to order
 * totals, and ensures integrity for reconciliation and compliance. Created
 * records support audit trails, downstream financial reporting, and refund
 * mechanics.
 *
 * Returns the full payment object after successful creation, including all
 * system-generated fields. Errors are returned for validation or permission
 * failures.
 *
 * @param props - Request props
 * @param props.admin - Authenticated admin account
 * @param props.orderId - UUID of the order for which a payment is being created
 * @param props.body - Payment creation details (IShoppingPayment.ICreate)
